<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-5198] PrincipalImpl is not part of the java API</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-5198</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The test class ShiroAuthenticationServiceTest uses the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/962289d83c9d9ec8d24c4a3851a99acccd5a39a0/zeppelin-server/src/test/java/org/apache/zeppelin/service/ShiroAuthenticationServiceTest.java#L78&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PrincipalImpl&lt;/a&gt; class, which is not part of the Java API.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;a href=&quot;https://rules.sonarsource.com/java/RSPEC-1191&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://rules.sonarsource.com/java/RSPEC-1191&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Classes in the sun.* or com.sun.* packages are considered implementation details, and are not part of the Java API.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They can cause problems when moving to new versions of Java because there is no backwards compatibility guarantee. Similarly, they can cause problems when moving to a different Java vendor, such as OpenJDK.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Such classes are almost always wrapped by Java API classes that should be used instead.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This implementation also triggers Maven warnings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
